WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.349
World loading now counts the shaders it builds, and says how smoothly the world will

00:00:07.349 --> 00:00:07.876
run.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.184
The programs are built in batches, each one counted, through the same pass the ride

00:00:15.184 --> 00:00:17.709
draws with, so nothing is built twice.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.431
Then the first frames warm up at the starting quality, and the card says the frame

00:00:27.431 --> 00:00:28.859
rate they held at Low.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.561
After twenty seconds without the world, the card says it is taking longer than

00:00:40.561 --> 00:00:41.713
usual, and why.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.969
Start at Low quality, ride with the panorama, or keep waiting; a build that fails

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:55.426
steps down a level.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:05.379
The warning and its choices, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.506
What the tests prove: the programs are counted, the frame rate is held, and a slow

00:01:19.506 --> 00:01:21.056
load offers a way out.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
